      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "From 1903 to 1937, the Bureau of Indian Affairs ran the Truxton Canyon Training School in Valentine, a boarding school for Native American children.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valentine%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Valentine lies on the former U.S. Route 66, 32 miles northeast of Kingman, and is a classic stop along the historic highway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valentine%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community is largely within an exclave of the Hualapai Reservation, with the rest in unincorporated Mohave County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valentine%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
